	"_doc": "Each place is a stack of parallax layers drawn back to front. 'kind' picks a placeholder drawer: hills, mountains, trees, pines, broadleaf, canopy, palms, mesas, cacti, water, ground, reeds, fronds, drifts, planet. 'parallax' is how fast the layer scrolls relative to the ground (1.0). 'y' and 'height' are fractions of the screen height. Optional per layer: 'snow' (white tips), 'foam' (surf on water), 'path' (the path colour on ground), 'craters'. Per place: 'icon' for its button, 'ambience' (a sound name), 'fx' (snow, wind, fireflies, stars), 'sky' to fix the sky instead of following the time of day, and 'fixed_light' to ignore the time of day's tint. Which level unlocks each place is in levels.json. Real art will replace the drawers with sprite chunks per layer.",
